woman gives birth. This approach should not be used with fertility rates that
are stratified by \code{union_type} because unpartnered fertility is what creates
the search. This approach is useful if the user has no particular interest in
union formation processes but wants to assign parentage correctly for kinship
determination.
\item The "rate" approach uses female marriage rates defined by
the \code{rates} argument. The input should be a marriage rate schedule that may
be stratified by group dimensions and/or \code{previous_union}. When stratified by
\code{previous_union}, remarriages may be duration-specific rather than
age-specific. This approach should generally be used with fertility rates
that are stratified by \code{union_type}, although it is not required. Failure to
stratify by \code{union_type} will lead to independence between fertility and
union formation.
}

Once a search is initiated, a woman will select a male partner from among all
eligible male partners. Men related to the women are considered ineligible
