It is possible for this search to fail if no eligible men are available. When
using the "on_demand" method, the \code{cancel_birth_if_no_match} argument
controls whether the birth continues if no match is found. If set to FALSE,
the birth continues but with \code{NA} values for the father. If set to TRUE,
observed fertility rates may deviate from input rates.

When unpartnered fertility is allowed, the \code{matching_model} will also be used
to identify the father of a birth to an unpartnered woman. Users can
optionally specify a separate \code{father_matching} model for this case.

Cohabitation can be added to the union formation process by specifying
\code{cohab_prob} and \code{union_convert_rate}. The \code{cohab_prob} argument expects a
data frame that is similar to a rate process object. It contains age-specific
bands defined by \code{age_start} and \code{age_end}, but also contains a \code{prob} column
rather than a \code{rate} column. This \code{prob} column defines the probability that
a union formed by a woman of the given age is a cohabitation instead of a
marriage. Like rate processes, \code{cohab_prob} can be stratified by time period
using \code{time_start} and \code{time_end}, group dimensions, or by \code{previous_union}.

